== Backward narrowing: compute the whole chain at K instead of W ==
   working width W = 12, consumer keeps K = 6 low bits
   chain: t1 = op(a,b); t2 = op(t1,c); r = op(t2,a); observed = r & mask(K)
   exhaustive over a,b,c in 0..2^12 would be 2^36 triples; this sweeps
   a,b exhaustively at 2^12 each and c over a fixed 64-value spread.

